{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1557739-fireamrs-vs-armored-structure","id":1557739,"title":"Fireamrs vs Armored structure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-18T15:11:03-08:00","id":1557739,"title":"Fireamrs vs Armored structure","content":"An exemple<br /> You have a shooter, he posess an assault rifle dealing 7lethal damage dice, his target is a light tank with 15 soaking dice on side. At first you say &quot;meh even with 3/4 success he's got small chance to damage it, it's just to tough&quot;... And then you realise the shooter is a (fictional for this exemple) 3rd gen vampire with dex 10, firearms 10 and celerity 10, scoring 16 success, getting 15 base damage dice with 7 more from the assault rifle, total 22 against an armored tank. Giving that vampire the ability to greatly damage thick steel plate with regular 7.62 bullets<br /> <br /> Question: Is the ST the one telling that assault rifle won't do any arm to the tank for obvious realistic reason or is there any actual rule in some book telling when a gun can or cannot damage structures or specific ennemy with specific powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T17:25:38-08:00","id":1557746,"title":"","content":"Ultimately it's going to be the ST since the WoD games largely ignored this subject. The idea of high powered characters using their super-high stats to turn mundane weapons against mundane armored vehicles just... wasn't something the games tried to emulate so the rules largely leave it to the ST to rule on based on the tone the ST wants to maintain for their instance of the game.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you're just using VtM books... were are you even finding stats for a tank? Pretty much Mage is the only game that gets into stats for things because you have Hypertech fleets of voidships storming mystical Umbral Realm with serious ground troops to combat Archmages to actually have the designers think about stating these sorts of things up.<br /> <br /> There are some simple solutions for STs that want to address this to a reasonable level without reworking the whole system (one I've used in the past is base damage of the weapon has to be greater than the armor rating of the target to deal damage; so no 16 successes to make a standard assault rifle do diddly to a tank).. but it's house-rule territory not RAW territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T02:40:32-08:00","id":1557754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1557739-fireamrs-vs-armored-structure?p=1557746#post1557746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately it's going to be the ST since the WoD games largely ignored this subject.<br /> There are some simple solutions for STs that want to address this to a reasonable level without reworking the whole system (one I've used in the past is base damage of the weapon has to be greater than the armor rating of the target to deal damage; so no 16 successes to make a standard assault rifle do diddly to a tank).. but it's house-rule territory not RAW territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what i thought, interesting houserule, by the way. Personnaly i thought about giving a specific &quot;armored&quot; condition to some specific structure and vehicule that indicate only antimaterial weapon (rocket launcher, antimaterial rifle, explosives like c4...) can damage.<br /> <br /> Since i've read Warhammer40k wrath and glory, Vampire the requiem 2nd edition and Werewolf the forsaken 2nd edition i fell for the conditions system x)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}